# casparcg-cef-api<NNNNN> for each -dev package below, set in debian/rules
Provides: ${cef:Provides}
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Description: chromiumembedded for casparcg-server
 Chromium Embedded Framework runtime. It provides casparcg-cef-api<NNNNN>
 for each CEF stable API version it is published for, which clients built
 against that API version depend on.

# One -dev package per CEF stable API version. Its name sets the version
# libcef_dll_wrapper is built for. Add another here to build another version.
Package: casparcg-cef-api15000-dev
Section: libdevel
Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
Depends: casparcg-cef (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Architecture: amd64 arm64
Description: chromiumembedded for casparcg-server - CEF stable API 15000
 Chromium Embedded Framework headers, and libcef_dll_wrapper built for CEF
 stable API version 15000. Use find_package(casparcg-cef-api15000 CONFIG)
 and link CasparCG::CEF.
